  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image-only, ResNet50) is very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality and suggesting the current best is RNA-based. The largest remaining uncertainty is whether the RNA representation itself can be substantially improved by switching from a linear PCA projection to a pretrained transformer encoder (scGPT). This experiment (config_007) isolates the encoder effect by keeping profile_setting=singleprofile and model_setting=rna_only identical to config_001, changing only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scGPT. If scGPT yields a meaningful gain, it redefines the RNA baseline and informs all downstream multimodal experiments; if it does not, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and remaining budget can focus on profile/aggregation/fusion dimensions. With 7 experiments left, resolving the encoder question early is the highest-value single-variable test before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

